<title>USA: Kiwi Airlines sees return to sky before Christmas.</title>
<headline>Kiwi Airlines sees return to sky before Christmas.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kiwi Airlines, which is presently bankrupt, said Wednesday it expected to resume flying before Christmas, using eight of its 15 planes.</p>
<p>The Newark, N.J.-based carrier, whose operations were suspended on Oct. 15, said it would make a further announcement on the matter at the end of next week. It said it expected to use 600 of its 1,200 furloughed staff members when it resumed flying.</p>
<p>Kiwi also said that a Florida-based company of investors called Wasatch Co. provided a previously announced $2.5 million instalment of a $5 million debtor-in-possession financing plan.</p>
<p>The financing was presented Wednesday in a U.S. Bankruptcy Court in Newark, N.J.</p>
